g per-share FCF and EPS mechanically."],"risks":["Revenue growth is decelerating (7.4% vs 7.8% prior quarter), and further deceleration below 2% would break the growth-quality part of the thesis.","Net debt/EBITDA of 1.9x combined with negative book equity leaves limited balance sheet cushion if FCF growth stalls.","Macro regime is split nearly evenly across Goldilocks/Reflation/Stagflation/Contraction (27.7/22.4/22.3/27.6), so a shift toward Stagflation or Contraction could pressure both fundamentals and the multiple simultaneously.","Weak short-term technical momentum (negative MACD, price below 20/50-day averages) suggests the market has not yet confirmed a bottom."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 2% (currently 7.4%)","ROIC falls below 26% (currently 34.7%)","Operating margin YoY change falls below -2.0 pts (currently +3.3 pts)","Technology rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (currently +68)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently 49.9% combined)","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength"],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Domain registrars, web hosting partners, and payment processors integrated into GoDaddy's commerce platform benefit if GoDaddy's FCF-funded reinvestment accelerates platform usage.","Small-business software and marketing tool providers that bundle with GoDaddy's hosting/domain ecosystem could see higher attach rates if GoDaddy sustains margin-driven reinvestment in its product suite.","Activist or value-oriented institutional investors may be drawn to the stock given the valuation/quality mismatch, potentially accelerating a re-rating."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"GDDY TTM revenue growth is 7.4%, down from 7.8% in the prior quarter","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin expanded 329 bps YoY to 24.8% and FCF grew 17.2%","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"GDDY trades at 13x P/E and 2.9x EV/Sales, in 